<code>assert 0 <= index && index <= \old(this.size()) && role != null => \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i)) || (\old(this.get(i)) == null && this.get(i) == null);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert 0 <= index && index <= \old(this.size()) && role != null => \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); this.get(i) == (\old(this.get(i)) == null ? null : \old(this.get(i)));</code>

This assertion ensures that for every position from the given index to the old size of the list, the element at the next position is either null (if the old element at that position was null) or it is equal to the old element at that position.
